Hey folks,

quick update to address a couple of issues arisen during these last few days:

 Fixed new occurrences of FirstLevelValidationFail, which were caused by multiplayer-related actions managed uproperly;
 Fixed new occurrences of NotEnoughResources related to work actions (Harvests and Productions);
 Improved the UI layout of some windows (e.g. New Offline Game) which had graphic issues on some aspect ratios;
 Added some shortcuts to better navigate through players boards/tables, as well as to open up the correct board in multiplayer matches;
 Improved the automatic tracking system during multiplayer matches.

Overall, this should help making all multiplayer sessions more stable, or at least aid us figuring out what's going on.

As always, drop by and leave a message should you need further support!
Take care

Hey folks,

here's another small update with some new fixes for you:

 Fixed error called CantHalfOddServantsBoost, which was related to not being able to add enough Servants while Excommunicated with the effect "You need two Servants to increase by 1 the value of your action;
 Fixed instances of the AI taking too much to think (where "too much" meant from 5 minutes to positive infinity);
 Machiavelli now works AND is displayed properly when his effects apply to harvests and productions. Say hi to Niccolò;
 Some minor usability fixes around, including the missing "different" symbol from the board game when you're getting more than one Council Privilege.


As always, thank you for your patience and for your support!
See you soon :)

Howdy, fellow players!

While we keep working on the AI performance in this unsettling world-wide scenario, here's a couple of hotfixes we were able to put our hands on:

 Fixed many different instances of FirstLevelValidationFail caused by leader activations and during the score calculation at the end of the match;
 Fixed weird animations overlaps caused by AIs at the beginning of new Eras, when AIs were first to play;
 Resolution settings in the Options menu had some unpredictable behaviours that we should have now fixed. This, unfortunately, does not include support for 21:9 screens so far, but it should be easier for these players to switch to other supported resolutions while they wait;
 Machiavelli had some issues in calculating the bonus score it gives; while there's still a minor issue in counting the bonus during Harvests and Productions that give score from multiple sources, the logic behind him has been fixed and we felt it was better to release it than not addressing the issue at all.


Many thanks to those who sent their bug reports on instances of FirstLevelValidationFail - your data was invaluable to fix it quickly and hopefully completely.
See you soon!

Howdy, a quick fix was released yesterday to address a couple of issues:

 We started working on the Sound FX system, so many sound feedbacks are now finally available to everyone;
 Activating a Leader while the Asset pick animation was still going now does not cause the game to get stuck;
 A new soft-lock during the 2nd tutorial was finally fixed;
 Fixed other AI errors related to various reported issues (WeakFamilyMember and FirstLevelValidationFail)
 Fixed a situation where, during Production, it was possible to spend more Servants than those actually owned.

Thanks again for the many user reports you are sending - they help us work like a breeze!

Finally a reason to rejoice on monday! This version brings a major rework to the bottom UI of the game, so that information is now clearer, prettier, and closer to our community expectations!

 Personal Territories and Buildings are now always shown;
 There's way more space for Assets information;
 Leaders are now always on screen;
 Camera movements does not impede seeing the farthest elements on the screen anymore;
 Turn order, Military Points, Vatican reports, opponents' preview and other minor screens have been polished according to your precious suggestions.


Please note: due to the massive changes, the tutorial is temporarily disabled. It's gonna come back as soon as we fix more pressing issues, hopefully along with many other improvements.

For a complete list of changes, as usual, visit our Trello board here.
And if you wanna reach out and share some feedback, stop by to say hi on the usual BoardGameGeek thread!
